            <ArticleTitle>An 8-year-old boy with bilateral lower extremity pain and weakness.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>872-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/PEC.0b013e31822c2896</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We illustrate a case of an 8-year-old boy presenting acutely with bilateral lower extremity pain and weakness. This case illustrates the presentation and progression of a rare and potentially lethal diagnosis and highlights the use of computed tomography angiography in the setting of a patient with acute onset of pain and pulselessness of the lower extremities.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
